      "message": "If the error is bigger than the pipe capacity, then this CL causes a deadlock. Can reproduce with the following and a \u003e4096 failure\n\n```\n--- a/android/virtmgr/src/crosvm.rs\n+++ b/android/virtmgr/src/crosvm.rs\n@@ -315,6 +315,11 @@ impl VmState {\n             let config \u003d *config;\n             let detect_hangup \u003d config.detect_hangup;\n             let (failure_pipe_read, failure_pipe_write) \u003d create_pipe()?;\n+            nix::fcntl::fcntl(\n+                failure_pipe_read.as_raw_fd(),\n+                nix::fcntl::FcntlArg::F_SETPIPE_SZ(4096),\n+            )\n+            .unwrap();\n             let vfio_devices \u003d config.vfio_devices.clone();\n             let tap \u003d\n                 if let Some(tap_file) \u003d \u0026config.tap { Some(tap_file.try_clone()?) } else { None };\n```\n\nThat is unlikely to happen since the default capacity is huge, but we should probably move the `failure_pipe_read` read before the `child.wait()` or put it in another thread.",
